B.a5S=new A.B("How do we arrange a fixture?","Create a match, pick the opposing school, and set the sport, age group, date and venue. They confirm, and it appears on both calendars.")
B.a51=new A.B("Who enters the score?","Either school can post the result. If the two entries disagree, both are flagged and neither counts towards the table until it is settled.")
B.a5N=new A.B("Can a result be corrected?","Yes. Corrections are kept on the record so tables can be recalculated and anyone following the match can see what changed.")
B.a44=new A.B("What happens to a postponed match?","Mark it postponed and it comes off the table until a new date is agreed. Everyone following the fixture is notified.")
B.W2=s([B.a5S,B.a51,B.a5N,B.a44],t.Wy)
B.a66=new A.az(B.hg,"Fixtures and results",B.W2)
B.or=new A.af(62889,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.a4k=new A.B("How are standings worked out?","Three points for a win, one for a draw. Schools level on points are split on score difference, then on points scored, then on their results against each other (head-to-head), then alphabetically.")
B.a4n=new A.B("Why is our table different from the rankings?","Tables cover one sport and age group. Rankings compare schools across everything they play, so a school strong in several sports climbs higher.")
B.a41=new A.B("What is the AI analysis?","A reading of past results - form, scoring margins and head-to-head - shown with the numbers behind it. It is a projection, not a prediction of what will happen.")
B.WC=s([B.a4k,B.a4n,B.a41],t.Wy)
